WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
Look down on Africa from space.

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.310
A green band of rainforest
runs along the equator.

3
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.750
To the north lies a vast
brown expanse: the Sahara,

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.130
a hot desert.

5
00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.930
Pull back, and the pattern repeats.

6
00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.210
Rainforests hug the equator.

7
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.630
Hot deserts lie further
out, north and south.

8
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.490
Why should rainforests and deserts
line up in bands like this?

9
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:25.810
Is it the oceans?

10
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.230
Is it the mountains?

11
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.490
In this mission, you'll see how
the Sun heats the Earth unevenly,

12
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:33.930
from the equator to the poles.

13
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.690
Then you'll build a model
of the whole planet,

14
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:38.630
one cell at a time.

15
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:43.970
Your mission: explain why rainforests
and hot deserts form bands either side of

16
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:44.830
the equator.
